title: Pubgrade
abstract: >-
  Pubgrade (Publish-Upgrade) is a publish-subscribe service that notifies
  deployments of new images of the software they run. A repository's CI
  publishes a new image to Pubgrade, which notifies all deployments that
  subscribed to the repository's tag or branch at the same time and records
  the result per subscriber; Pubgrade-Sidecar, next to a Kubernetes
  Deployment, then updates its image. It is built with FOCA and deployed to
  Kubernetes or OpenShift with its Helm chart.
